        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A zero turn is the best time-saving tool in residential lawn care when the ground is flat and the yard is full of things to mow around. Put it on steep or wet slopes, or ask it to haul heavy loads, and its central design choice becomes a liability.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A lawn tractor is slower and leaves more trimming, but it is cheaper, safer on hills and does more jobs. Count your obstacles, measure your worst slope and list your other chores, and the right machine is usually obvious.
          </p>
        </div>

